title: StarDialogue
---
Star: ..Sasha?
Star: What are you doing here?
-> What's going on?
-> Oh.. my head hurts..
Star: No.. no-no-no! This won't do, this just won't do. You've come way too early, you're much too fast. You're not supposed to be here at all!
Star: I haven't had enough time to prepare! It's still a work-in-progress, my dear. I haven't had enough time to adjust and assimilate..
Star: Do you always appear before the curtain call?

-> Who are you?

Star: Star.

-> Star?

Star: The Void Mother, or so people are starting to call me.

-> Am I dead?
-> So I've died.

Star: Far from dead- perhaps more alive now than ever. Hm.. let me see you, lift your head to face mine- yes, just like that, my doll. Let me see your eyes..
Star: Hm..
Star: Interesting, very interesting..

-> What is it?
-> I don't like you playing these games, out with it!

Star: Have you ever considered, Sasha, how incomplete we all are? Yet we are all attempting to make sense of this incompletion through faith and worship rather than true being.
Star: Yet you.. you chose faith through a trust in the system that I weaved for you. Was that because you sought to be completed? Or something else?

-> Are you god?
    Star: No.
    -> What's the point, then?
-> What are you talking about?
    Star: Is it my duty to explain it to you? Or is it yours to take your own understanding from my words?
    -> What's the point, then?

Star: I am as much a vessel of an idea as you are the person who walked on stage unannounced and uninvited. We both, in essence, sought the same thing.
Star: I feel uncomfortable to notice that I have become revered for it.

-> What is that?

Star: Amusement.

-> Why am I here, then?
-> I don't see how that makes me the same as you.

Star: It is because you entered - uninvited by me, though perhaps others - into a place that was not yet finished. Your goal, the island, was not ready for you which you were perhaps marginally aware of. After all, the scope would have been too big for a mere nine weeks.. Yet, you went anyway.
Star: Perhaps my goal here is to tell you that it isn't ready yet, but that is truly up for you to decide. I am a concept as much as I exist in truth.
Star: You exist as a being solely to do so, to live and to breathe and to experience my creation. Perhaps that's why you went- though I'm only spitballing here.
Star: But.. Don't see my word as true fact. What is your purpose, Sasha?
<<askPlayerForPurpose>>

===
title: afterpurpose
---
Star: I see..
Star: It is not up to me to decide whether I agree with your vision or not. All I can say is that I simply do not know.
Star: Rome was not built in a day, as the small-minded say. I'm still working on my metaphors..
Star: But Sasha.. My dearest, do not rush me. I am only an assimilation of nine voices, and so, I must continue to spin this story as I live and see fit. Patience is both a virtue and a blessing you have been born to live with.
Star: Go home now my child, let it all start again in due time.

===



